~ Lava — the bound forms. Symbols, because a bound is read at a glance:
~   >= <N|C>  >  <N|C>  <= <N|C>  <  <N|C>  between <N|C> and <N|C>
~ >= <= between include their endpoints; > < exclude them.

~ inclusive range — 0 and 100 are both legal values
create container "Temp" of type int between 0 and 100 with value 0
print(Temp)
update Temp to 100
print(Temp)

~ strict minimum: 0 would be rejected, 1 is the smallest legal value
create container "Quantity" of type int > 0 with value 1
print(Quantity)

~ strict maximum against another container — Ceiling itself is out of range
create container "Ceiling" of type int with value 10
create container "Draw" of type int < Ceiling with value 9
print(Draw)

~ clauses join with `and`; this is exactly `between 1 and 12`
create container "Month" of type int >= 1 and <= 12 with value 12
print(Month)

~ the strict bound bites here: 0 is not greater than 0, so this write fails
update Quantity to 0
print("never reached")
